{"id":"s2.1.8","slug":"pi-and-e-approximations","title":"π and e Approximations","content":"<p class=\"mb-4\">Using standard approximations for π (≈ 3.1) and e (≈ 2.7) can lead to several other useful values for estimation problems (which typically have a ±5% margin of error).</p><ul class=\"list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mb-4\"><li><strong>π² ≈ 10</strong></li><li><strong>e³ ≈ 20</strong></li><li><strong>πe ≈ 8.5</strong></li><li><strong>e² ≈ 7.4</strong></li></ul><p>Knowing these allows you to quickly approximate more complex expressions. For example, $(e \\times \\pi)^4 = e^4 \\times \\pi^4 = e \\cdot e^3 \\cdot (\\pi^2)^2 \\approx 2.7 \\times 20 \\times 10^2 = 5400$.</p>","summary":"Using standard approximations for π (≈ 3.1) and e (≈ 2.7) can lead to several other useful values for estimation problems (which typically have a ±5% margin of error).","generation_guideline":"Generate an approximation problem involving powers or products of π and e.","questions":[{"id":1,"text":"Calculate $2\\pi^4$.","answer":"194","kind":"approximate","tags":["arithmetic"],"hasErrorRange":true},{"id":2,"text":"Calculate $e^2 \\times \\pi^4$.","answer":"722","kind":"approximate","tags":["arithmetic"],"hasErrorRange":true},{"id":3,"text":"Calculate $e^4$.","answer":"54","kind":"approximate","tags":["arithmetic"],"hasErrorRange":true},{"id":4,"text":"Calculate $\\pi^5$.","answer":"306","kind":"approximate","tags":["arithmetic"],"hasErrorRange":true},{"id":5,"text":"Calculate $(e \\times \\pi)^4$.","answer":"5329","kind":"approximate","tags":["arithmetic"],"hasErrorRange":true},{"id":6,"text":"Calculate $\\pi^5 + e^4$.","answer":"360","kind":"approximate","tags":["arithmetic"],"hasErrorRange":true},{"id":7,"text":"Calculate $\\pi^3 \\times e^4$.","answer":"1695","kind":"approximate","tags":["arithmetic"],"hasErrorRange":true},{"id":8,"text":"Calculate $(3\\pi)^4$.","answer":"7873","kind":"approximate","tags":["arithmetic"],"hasErrorRange":true},{"id":9,"text":"Calculate $(e + 1.3)^5$.","answer":"1048","kind":"approximate","tags":["arithmetic"],"hasErrorRange":true},{"id":10,"text":"Calculate $[(\\pi - .2)(e + .3)]^3$.","answer":"699","kind":"approximate","tags":["arithmetic"],"hasErrorRange":true},{"id":11,"text":"Calculate $(\\pi + 1.9)^3(e + 2.3)^3$.","answer":"16194","kind":"approximate","tags":["arithmetic"],"hasErrorRange":true},{"id":12,"text":"Calculate $(4e)^3$.","answer":"1277","kind":"approximate","tags":["arithmetic"],"hasErrorRange":true},{"id":13,"text":"Calculate $e^4\\pi^4$.","answer":"5329","kind":"approximate","tags":["arithmetic"],"hasErrorRange":true},{"id":14,"text":"Calculate $\\pi^e e^\\pi$.","answer":"518","kind":"approximate","tags":["arithmetic"],"hasErrorRange":true},{"id":15,"text":"Calculate $(3\\pi + 2e)^4$.","answer":"48774","kind":"approximate","tags":["arithmetic"],"hasErrorRange":true},{"id":16,"text":"Calculate $\\pi^\\pi e^e$.","answer":"552","kind":"approximate","tags":["arithmetic"],"hasErrorRange":true}]}